# Python
# pytest writes these on every local `python3 -m pytest tools/tests` run; they were
# tracked until now, so a test run dirtied the tree with binary noise before each commit.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Ant junitlauncher
# The `legacy-plain` listener writes one TEST-<class>.txt per class into the basedir.
# ci-test does not use it -- it uses TestFailureReportingListener -- so a normal run
# produces none of these. They appear when someone adds a temporary single-class target
# to debug one test, which is a documented habit here, and then `git add -A` sweeps them
# into the commit. Three reached main that way (e9dc151e, 516f94dc) before this line.
TEST-*.txt
